{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV4TiedV4kindAA12MXLStartStopOvp","role":"symbol","title":"kind","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this element marks the start or the stop of the tie."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct\/kind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/kind"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStop","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStop":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStop","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStartStop","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstop","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStop","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStartStop","abstract":[{"text":"The start-stop type is used for an attribute of musical elements that can either start or stop, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuplets.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct/kind":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStartStopO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStop"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct\/kind","title":"kind","abstract":[{"text":"Whether this element marks the start or the stop of the tie.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome.Note","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Tied","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-tied indicates the presence of a tie within a metric relationship mark. As with the tied"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, both the start and stop of the tie should be specified, in this case within separate metronome-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}]}}}